# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clara — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your own keys:
#     cp .env.example .env.local
# `.env.local` is gitignored and never committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED — Anthropic API key (powers letter understanding).
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# The Anthropic SDK reads this variable automatically.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key-here

# REQUIRED for audio — ElevenLabs API key (text-to-speech read-aloud).
# Get one at https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
# Without this, letter processing still works but the "listen" audio will fail.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your-elevenlabs-api-key-here

# OPTIONAL — ElevenLabs voice ID.
# Leave unset to use Clara's built-in per-language default voices.
# Free-tier ElevenLabs accounts cannot use shared library voices via the API,
# so set this to a voice your account owns (a Default Voice or a cloned one).
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=your-voice-id-here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE
# By default Clara stores everything in a local SQLite file at ./data/clara.db
# — no configuration needed, nothing to set here.
#
# If you fork Clara to run against an external database (e.g. Postgres),
# set your connection string here and wire it up in lib/db.ts.
# See the "Connect a database" section of the README for a walkthrough.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/clara
